<decompilertest>
<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:windows">
<!--
    kuna calleeretpreserves: an MSVC /GS caller loses the zero it set before the
    frame-cookie check, and the call it makes acquires a return value the machine
    never computes.

    x86-64-win.cspec lists RAX in <killedbycall> for the default __fastcall, so
    Heritage::guardCalls (heritage.cc:1444) plants an INDIRECT creation of RAX at
    every call and registers a return trial for it.  That is an answer about the
    CONVENTION.  __security_check_cookie contradicts it: its returning path is
    "cmp rcx,[cookie]; rol rcx,0x10; test cx,0xffff; ret" and it never touches
    RAX, which is exactly why MSVC sets EAX before the call rather than after it.

    f, at 0x1000, is that shape reduced to the seam:

        1000  48 83 ec 28     SUB   RSP,0x28
        1004  33 c0           XOR   EAX,EAX          ; the value f returns
        1006  48 83 c1 01     ADD   RCX,0x1
        100a  e8 f1 00 00 00  CALL  0x1100           ; the cookie checker
        100f  48 83 c4 28     ADD   RSP,0x28
        1013  c3              RET

    and 0x1100 is __security_check_cookie's body verbatim, with its failure path
    leaving by the same direct JMP into a __fastfail stub:

        1100  48 3b 0d f9 ..  CMP   RCX,[0x1200]
        1107  75 10           JNZ   0x1119
        1109  48 c1 c1 10     ROL   RCX,0x10
        110d  66 f7 c1 ff ff  TEST  CX,0xffff
        1112  75 01           JNZ   0x1115
        1114  c3              RET
        1115  48 c1 c9 10     ROR   RCX,0x10
        1119  e9 12 00 00 00  JMP   0x1130
        1130  b9 02 00 00 00  MOV   ECX,0x2
        1135  cd 29           INT   0x29             ; __fastfail, never returns
        1137  c3              RET

    The int 0x29 is why the callee-body write probe has to know about
    fastfailnoreturn: x86 SLEIGH lifts INT imm8 to "intloc = swi(imm8);
    call [intloc]" (ia.sinc:3671), and an unrecognized indirect call makes the
    walk declare itself incomplete, which proves nothing about RAX.

    g, at 0x1400, is the NEGATIVE control and has f's shape exactly, except that
    its callee at 0x1410 is "endbr64; ret" - a stub, which is also what a
    placeholder and an entry decoded at the wrong address look like.  Its silence
    about RAX is not evidence, so g must render identically in both passes.

    Stage: P3 heritage call guarding, option calleeretpreserves off|on.  Pass 1
    (off) pins the bug, pass 2 (on, the default) pins the fix.
-->
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1000">
4883ec2833c04883c101e8f10000004883c428c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1100">
483b0df9000000751048c1c11066f7c1ffff7501c348c1c910e912000000
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1130">
b902000000cd29c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1200">
efcdab8967452301
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1400">
4883ec2833c0e8050000004883c428c3
</bytechunk>
<bytechunk space="ram" offset="0x1410">
f30f1efac3
</bytechunk>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1000" name="f"/>
<symbol space="ram" offset="0x1400" name="g"/>
</binaryimage>
<script>
  <com>option calleeretpreserves off</com>
  <com>lo fu f</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu g</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>option calleeretpreserves on</com>
  <com>lo fu f</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>lo fu g</com>
  <com>decompile</com>
  <com>print C</com>
  <com>quit</com>
</script>
<stringmatch name="CALLEERETPRESERVES #1: off, the zero set before the cookie check is gone and f returns nothing" min="1" max="1">^void f\(int8 a0\)$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEERETPRESERVES #2: on, f returns the constant the caller placed in EAX" min="1" max="1">^  return 0;$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEERETPRESERVES #3: on, and that value gives f its own return type back" min="1" max="1">^unsigned long long f\(int8 a0\)$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEERETPRESERVES #4: both passes, the checker is still called with the same argument" min="2" max="2">^  sub_1100\(a0 \+ 1\);$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEERETPRESERVES #5: both passes, an endbr64/ret stub proves nothing and g is unchanged" min="2" max="2">^void g\(void\)$</stringmatch>
<stringmatch name="CALLEERETPRESERVES #6: both passes, the stub call keeps the convention's answer" min="2" max="2">^  sub_1410\(\);$</stringmatch>
</decompilertest>
